### 4.1 Why this layout

- **`.claude/steering/`** is project memory — imported into `CLAUDE.md` via `@`-imports so it loads on every session.
- **`.claude/rules/`** and **`.claude/templates/`** are the *style guide* for how the agent generates artifacts. Treat them as code-reviewed configuration.
- **`.mcp.json`** at the repo root declares project-scope MCP servers. User-scope MCP lives in `~/.claude.json` (or is added with `claude mcp add --scope user`).
- **`.claude/settings.json`** holds the permission allow/deny lists, hooks, and environment. Personal overrides go in `.claude/settings.local.json` (gitignored).
- **`specs/`** at the repo root is the living technical history of every approved contract.
- **`.claude/skills/`** contains the executable workflow as Agent Skills.
- **`.claude/agents/`** contains custom sub-agent definitions (reviewer, debugger, etc.).
- **`CLAUDE.md`** is the entry-point Claude Code reads automatically; it imports steering and points to this guide.

### 4.2 Minimum per-repository checklist

Every repository that uses this workflow SHALL have, at a minimum:

- `.claude/steering/{product,tech,structure}.md`
- `.claude/steering/{security,testing,api-conventions}.md` for any non-trivial codebase
- `CLAUDE.md` importing every steering file (always-on) and pointing to this guide
- `.claude/settings.json` with permission allow/deny lists scoped to read/validation by default
- `.gitignore` covering secrets and credentials
- `.mcp.json` declaring only the project-specific MCP servers that are reviewed and approved

Keeping a workspace current: `csdd update` refreshes the csdd-managed artifacts (rules, versioned templates, shipped skills/agents/commands/hooks, this guide, `csdd.md`) to the installed binary's version. It reconciles against `.claude/.csdd-manifest.json` — a generated content-hash baseline that SHALL NOT be hand-edited — so pristine files are refreshed in place while any file you edited is preserved as a numbered `<file>-N.old` backup before the new version lands. It never touches `specs/`, your filled steering, custom skills/agents, `.mcp.json`, `settings.json`, or `CLAUDE.md`. Run `csdd update --dry-run` to preview.

