## 13. Best practices by stack

### 13.1 TypeScript/JavaScript

Recommended steering:

- `tsconfig` patterns.
- ESLint/Prettier.
- Module structure.
- Conventions for React/Next/Vite/Node.
- Unit/integration/e2e test patterns; test-first policy.
- Type policy: avoid `any`, prefer explicit types at boundaries.
- Rules for package managers and monorepos.

Useful hook commands (wire into `Stop` / `PostToolUse`):

```bash
npm run lint
npm run typecheck
npm test
npm run build
```

### 13.2 Python

Recommended steering:

- Minimum Python version.
- Use of venv/poetry/uv/pip according to team standards.
- Lint/format with ruff/black/mypy, if used.
- Package structure.
- pytest conventions; write the failing test first.
- Typing and input validation.

Useful hook commands:

```bash
python -m pytest
ruff check .
ruff format --check .
mypy .
```

### 13.3 Java

Recommended steering:

- Supported JDK.
- Maven/Gradle.
- Spring/Quarkus/Micronaut patterns when applicable.
- Unit and integration tests (test-first).
- Package conventions.
- Exception handling.
- Logging and observability.

Useful hook commands:

```bash
mvn test
mvn verify
./gradlew test
./gradlew check
```

