## 15. Operational checklists

### 15.1 Before starting a spec

- [ ] Clear goal.
- [ ] Scope and out-of-scope defined.
- [ ] Users/personas defined.
- [ ] Success criteria defined.
- [ ] Security/privacy requirements mapped.
- [ ] Known edge cases listed.
- [ ] External dependencies identified.
- [ ] Steering updated.

### 15.2 Before approving requirements

- [ ] Numeric IDs are present and unique.
- [ ] Every requirement uses EARS phrasing.
- [ ] Acceptance criteria are testable and single-behavior.
- [ ] Error cases and edge cases are covered.
- [ ] No implementation language ("how") — only behavior ("what").
- [ ] Non-functional requirements (performance, security, observability) are present.
- [ ] Compatibility and migration considered.
- [ ] Ambiguities resolved.

### 15.3 Before approving design

- [ ] Architecture consistent with `tech.md` and `structure.md`.
- [ ] Architecture Pattern & Boundary Map (Mermaid) is present.
- [ ] File Structure Plan is fully populated and matches the boundary map.
- [ ] Every requirement appears in the Requirements Traceability table.
- [ ] Every component has Intent, Requirements, Responsibilities, Dependencies, Contract.
- [ ] Errors, timeouts, retries, idempotency are addressed.
- [ ] Observability is included.
- [ ] Rollout/rollback strategy when needed.
- [ ] Testing strategy declares the TDD ordering.
- [ ] Trade-offs documented.

### 15.4 Before approving tasks

- [ ] Tasks are small (1–3 hours per sub-task).
- [ ] Phase ordering: Foundation → Core → Integration → Validation.
- [ ] Test-first sub-tasks precede their implementation sub-tasks.
- [ ] `_Requirements:_` is present on every task, with numeric IDs only.
- [ ] `_Boundary:_` is present on every `(P)` task and matches a component in `design.md`.
- [ ] `_Depends:_` is declared only for cross-boundary dependencies.
- [ ] Parallel safety is verified by `tasks-parallel-analysis.md`.
- [ ] Validation commands defined.
- [ ] Optional tasks marked.
- [ ] Clear completion criteria.

### 15.5 Before claiming completion

- [ ] `sdd-verify-completion` ran and produced fresh evidence.
- [ ] All tests pass (and each was red before its implementation); no `.skip` left behind without an explicit ticket.
- [ ] `spec.json` reflects current phase and approvals.
- [ ] Implementation Notes captured in `tasks.md` for cross-task learnings.

### 15.6 Security checklist

- [ ] `.gitignore` and permission deny rules configured before exposing the repo to the agent.
- [ ] No secrets in steering, specs, prompts, or skill files.
- [ ] MCP servers and tools reviewed; tool access allowlisted, not blanket-approved.
- [ ] Permission allow list is read/validation only by default; destructive patterns denied.
- [ ] Environment free of unnecessary credentials.
- [ ] Sensitive data masked when context is unavoidable.
- [ ] PR reviewed by a human.

### 15.7 CI/CD with headless CLI checklist

- [ ] `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` stored as a secret.
- [ ] Job uses a restricted `--allowed-tools` list (e.g., `Read,Grep,Glob`).
- [ ] Prompt is objective.
- [ ] Context is passed via pipe or controlled file.
- [ ] Job does not write code without an explicit policy.
- [ ] Required MCP servers fail the job fast if they do not start.
- [ ] Logs do not contain secrets.

