## 16. Reusable prompts

### 16.1 Create a feature spec (requirements-first)

```text
Create a requirements-first spec for [name].
Goal: [goal].
Users: [personas].
Scope: [included].
Out of scope: [excluded].
Acceptance criteria: [list].
Constraints: [security, performance, compliance, integration].
Edge cases: [list].
Before design, point out ambiguities and open questions.
```

### 16.2 Create a design-first spec

```text
Create a design-first spec for [technical goal].
Desired architecture: [description].
Required stack: [stack].
Constraints: [latency, throughput, cost, compliance, compatibility].
Integrations: [services/APIs].
Expected interfaces: [contracts].
Testing strategy: [unit/integration/e2e/property-based], written test-first.
Rollout/rollback strategy: [plan].
```

### 16.3 Analyze requirements

```text
Analyze the requirements of this spec.
Look for ambiguities, conflicts, non-testable requirements, missing edge cases,
security impacts, and undeclared dependencies.
Reply with: problem, severity, why it matters, and adjustment suggestion.
```

### 16.4 Review design

```text
Review the design of this spec against the steering files product.md, tech.md,
structure.md, security.md, and testing.md.
Check adherence to architecture, risks, testability, observability, rollback,
and trade-offs. Use plan mode; do not implement code yet.
```

### 16.5 Create a Bugfix Spec

```text
Create a Bugfix Spec for the problem below.
Symptom: [description].
Reproduction steps: [steps].
Current behavior: [current].
Expected behavior: [expected].
Behaviors that MUST NOT change: [list].
Logs/evidence: [logs].
First investigate the root cause, then write a failing regression test,
then propose design and tasks.
```

### 16.6 Review a diff

```text
Review the current changes (@<files> or the staged diff).
Evaluate correctness, security, regressions, tests, readability, adherence to
steering, and performance impact.
Reply in code review format: finding, severity, evidence, recommendation.
```

### 16.7 Implement a task with TDD

```text
Implement task <id> from @specs/<feature>/tasks.md.
Work test-first:
1. Write a failing test for the acceptance criteria; run it and confirm it fails
   for the expected reason.
2. Implement the minimum code to make it pass.
3. Refactor under green; run the focused test, then the fuller suite.
Do not change unrelated code. Record learnings in tasks.md ## Implementation Notes.
```

### 16.8 Generate tests

```text
Based on @<file> and the active spec, generate failing tests for acceptance
criteria not yet covered (red step).
Include success, error, edge, and regression cases.
Do not change production implementation without asking for confirmation.
```

