## 17. Adoption plan

### Phase 1 — Foundations (week 1)

- [ ] Run `npx @protonspy/csdd init` to scaffold `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/`, `specs/`, rules, templates, skills, and this guide.
- [ ] Configure `.gitignore` and permission deny rules for protected paths.
- [ ] Generate foundational steering: `product.md`, `tech.md`, `structure.md`; confirm they are imported into `CLAUDE.md`.
- [ ] Configure required MCP servers at the correct scope (project vs user).
- [ ] Define the permission allow list (read/validation only) and deny list in `.claude/settings.json`.
- [ ] Run one pilot spec end-to-end (small, low-risk feature) using the TDD loop.

### Phase 2 — Standardization (weeks 2–3)

- [ ] Add domain-specific steering: `security.md`, `api-conventions.md`, `testing.md`, `observability.md`.
- [ ] Customize templates in `.claude/templates/` for team conventions.
- [ ] Adopt phase-gate review in PR templates.
- [ ] Add lint/test hooks (`PostToolUse` formatter, `Stop` test gate, `PreToolUse` destructive-command guard).
- [ ] Define MCP and permission policy.
- [ ] Create custom sub-agents in `.claude/agents/` for review/test/debug.

### Phase 3 — Automation (weeks 4–6)

- [ ] Enable `/sdd-impl` autonomous mode (e.g., `acceptEdits`) for low-risk features.
- [ ] Add a CI workflow for headless `claude -p` review with `--allowed-tools`.
- [ ] Wire validation gates (`/sdd-validate-impl`) into the PR pipeline.
- [ ] Configure headless CLI review in PRs.
- [ ] Create internal plugins for company standards and publish them to an internal marketplace.

### Phase 4 — Continuous governance (ongoing)

- [ ] Audit usage and skill execution time.
- [ ] Review and rotate permission rules and MCP servers.
- [ ] Measure quality: PR cycle time, post-merge regressions, test coverage per critical feature.
- [ ] Update steering on every architectural change.

