## 23. Compliance summary

This document is the canonical specification for any Claude Code SDD workflow developed by the team. By the time a workflow is delivered, the following SHALL be true:

- All steering files exist and are imported into `CLAUDE.md` (always-on), with inclusion frontmatter documenting intended scope.
- All specs use EARS for requirements and the boundary-annotated format for tasks, with test-first sub-task pairing.
- All implementation followed the red → green → refactor loop; tests were red before the code that satisfied them.
- All skills conform to the `SKILL.md` template, the 500-line limit, and the progressive-disclosure rule for references.
- All MCP servers are reviewed, scoped, and free of versioned credentials.
- All hooks declare a single responsibility and run idempotent shell commands.
- All custom sub-agents declare the smallest tool scope required.
- `.gitignore` plus permission deny rules cover secrets, customer data, and large artifacts.
- All PRs link back to a spec or document why no spec was required.
- Approvals in `spec.json` reflect actual human review at each phase gate.

Any workflow that does not meet these requirements is not considered production-ready under this specification.

---

## 24. Versioning

This document SHALL be versioned with the repository. Major revisions follow these rules:

- **Major version (X.0)** — Breaking changes to the artifact model, phase-gate sequence, or skill structure.
- **Minor version (X.Y)** — New mandatory checklists, new required steering files, new skill conventions.
- **Patch version (X.Y.Z)** — Clarifications, additional examples, typo and link corrections.

Every revision SHALL include:

- A changelog entry summarizing the changes.
- An updated `Date` in the header.
- A note in the PR description on whether existing repositories need migration.
